// endpoint_post_to_slack_thread.proto — PostToSlackThread: post a reply into
// a subscribed Slack thread for a workspace. AGENT API section.
//
// WHAT IS POSTED. The text, under a small banner naming agent-repl and the
// workspace, and above a footer carrying the post's nonce, which is recorded
// before the post is sent, so the post is never told back to the workspace
// (slack_thread.proto). Every raw link in the text is posted as it is written.
//
// WHAT IS REFUSED. A post must open with exactly one Slack emoji shortcode
// chosen for what the post says (`:white_check_mark: tests pass`), then a
// space; the `:peepo_*:` shortcodes are the daemon's own announcements and
// are refused to agents. A text carrying what reads as a secret (an access
// key, a token, a private key) is refused and never sent. A listen-mode
// subscription refuses an unforced post, and so does one that reached its
// post limit (SlackThreadPosts).

